WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.097
In fields like healthcare and education we cannot
experiment freely,

00:00:04.177 --> 00:00:09.563
so offline reinforcement learning must learn the
environment's transition dynamics purely

00:00:09.643 --> 00:00:12.204
from a fixed batch of collected experience.

00:00:12.284 --> 00:00:17.548
The trouble is that this data only covers the
actions the original users actually took,

00:00:17.628 --> 00:00:20.619
leaving much of the state and action space unseen.

00:00:20.699 --> 00:00:25.839
Standard maximum likelihood estimates of the
dynamics therefore produce policies that

00:00:25.919 --> 00:00:31.122
swing wildly from dataset to dataset and can
recommend genuinely unsafe actions in the

00:00:31.202 --> 00:00:32.780
regions where data is thin.
